# Copy this file to `.env` and fill in your OWN keys:
#
#     cp .env.example .env
#
# `.env` is git-ignored — never commit it, never paste a key into chat, a
# ticket, or a screenshot. Every developer provisions their own keys; see the
# quota note against each one for why sharing a single key is a bad trade here.
#
# The pipeline reads these via python-dotenv (config.py loads .env automatically
# if it is installed). You can also export them in your shell instead.


# --- YouTube Data API v3 -----------------------------------------------------
# Needed by: run.py --provider youtube   (the main collection path)
# Get one:   https://console.cloud.google.com/
#   1. Create a project (or pick an existing one).
#   2. APIs & Services -> Library -> enable "YouTube Data API v3".
#   3. APIs & Services -> Credentials -> Create credentials -> API key.
#   4. Restrict the key to the YouTube Data API v3 before using it.
# Free, no billing account required.
#
# QUOTA IS PER KEY: ~10,000 units/day, and one country's full sweep costs
# ~3,600. One shared key = the whole team fights over 2-3 countries/day. Four
# developers with four keys = 8-12 countries/day. Provision individually.
YOUTUBE_API_KEY=


# --- SerpApi (Google Hotels + Tripadvisor reviews) ---------------------------
# Needed by: run.py --provider serpapi_reviews
# Get one:   https://serpapi.com/users/sign_up  -> dashboard -> "Your API Key"
#
# QUOTA IS PER ACCOUNT: 250 searches/month on the free tier. The adapter
# hard-caps each run at MAX_API_CALLS_PER_RUN (20) so one run cannot drain the
# month, but a shared key still burns down a single 250 allowance for everyone.
SERPAPI_KEY=


# --- Reddit (PRAW) -----------------------------------------------------------
# Needed by: run.py --provider reddit
# Get one:   https://www.reddit.com/prefs/apps -> "create another app..."
#   - choose type "script"
#   - redirect uri: http://localhost:8080  (unused, but required)
#   - client id is the string under the app name; secret is labelled "secret"
#
# The user agent must identify you — Reddit rate-limits generic ones harshly.
REDDIT_CLIENT_ID=
REDDIT_CLIENT_SECRET=
REDDIT_USER_AGENT=tourism-sentiment by u/your-reddit-username
